From: substrate
Subject: configure: assume run-tests pass when cross-building for substrate

auto/feature compiles a probe and, for ngx_feature_run=yes/value/bug,
RUNS it to decide whether the feature exists.  Cross-compiling to
substrate can't run the probe, so every run-test reports "found but
is not working" and the feature is disabled -- including the shared
memory primitives (MAP_ANON / MAP_DEVZERO / SysV shm / POSIX sem)
that nginx needs for its shared zones.

When NGX_PLATFORM is substrate:*, treat a successful compile+link as
proof the feature exists (the standard cross-compile assumption):
  - yes  -> found
  - value-> found, define name to ${ngx_feature_value:-1}
  - bug  -> assume the defect is absent (not found)

--- a/auto/feature
+++ b/auto/feature
@@ -49,6 +49,39 @@
 
 if [ -x $NGX_AUTOTEST ]; then
 
+  case "$NGX_PLATFORM" in
+    substrate:*)
+        # Cross-build: cannot execute the test binary on the host.  Treat a
+        # successful compile+link as proof the feature exists.
+        case "$ngx_feature_run" in
+            value)
+                echo " found (substrate assume)"
+                ngx_found=yes
+                cat << END >> $NGX_AUTO_CONFIG_H
+
+#ifndef $ngx_feature_name
+#define $ngx_feature_name  ${ngx_feature_value:-1}
+#endif
+
+END
+            ;;
+            bug)
+                # bug-tests look for a defect by crashing; assume no defect.
+                echo " not found"
+            ;;
+            *)
+                echo " found (substrate assume)"
+                ngx_found=yes
+                if test -n "$ngx_feature_name"; then
+                    have=$ngx_have_feature . auto/have
+                fi
+            ;;
+        esac
+        rm -rf $NGX_AUTOTEST*
+        return 0 2>/dev/null || true
+    ;;
+  esac
+
     case "$ngx_feature_run" in
 
         yes)
